@ 6.1.1 - Proto-Omotic to North Omotic
# citation: Mecislau, from Ehret, Christopher (1995), Reconstructing Proto-Afroasiatic (Proto-Afrasian): Vowels, Tone, Consonants, and Vocabulary (Voices from Asia)
	u o > i e
	e > i / #N_C
	e > i / #l_{P,C:[+ voice]}
	e > i / #b_
	e > i / p_r
	e > i / #{s,ʃ,tsʼ}_{k(w),ʔ}
	e o > i u / #C_P
	e o > i u / #(ʔ)_C
	e o > i u / #{k(ʼ),x}_{t(ʼ),tsʼ}
	e o > i u / #(ʔ)_C$
	e o > i u / #P_{tsʼ,tʃʼ}
	a > o / #{z,dʒ}_P
	{ e, e:[+ long] } > { i, i:[+ long] } / #C:[+sibilant]_{d,n,r}
	Cw > C
	V:[+ long] > V / #K:[-voice]_C
	u > u:[+ long] / #S:[+voice]_P:[-voice]
	V:[+ long] > V / #C_C$ + $(V)C$ suffix
	N > ∅ / V_{C:[+sibilant],p}